  "finalText": "Now the letter hops and idle wiggle.\nI built the \"Boop!\" intro in the Motion editor: 5 seconds at 1080×1080 and 60fps, on a cream background. I checked it with a contact sheet and it plays through as planned. I didn't run the critic or propose a storyboard first, so I haven't reviewed the pacing beyond that.\n\n- **Candy drop (0.1–2.4s):** Six shapes fall in one after another: **Pink circle**, **Yellow star**, **Blue square**, **Teal circle**, **Orange star** and **Purple square**. Each one stretches as it falls, squashes flat on landing, bounces twice and settles with a springy overshoot. They are pinned at the bottom so the squash stays grounded.\n- **Jostle (~1.8–2.6s):** Every shape gets a quick rotation kick, so they look like they bump each other.\n- **Letters (2.0–4.1s):** **B, o, o, p, !** hop in one at a time, 0.18s apart. Each launches up from below, comes down with a squash, takes one more smaller bounce and settles with a spring.\n- **Idle wiggle (to 5s):** The shapes wiggle gently from the start, and each letter starts wiggling once it has settled.\n\nThe letters came out a little smaller than I planned. I can make them bigger, change the colours, speed up the hops, or add a closing pulse on the last frame if you like."
